<title>BELGIUM: Generale Bank sees similar second half.</title>
<headline>Generale Bank sees similar second half.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Generale Bank NV, Belgium's biggest bank, said it expected second-half 1996 earnings to be in line with the first half of this year.</p>
<p>&quot;In view of the favourable economic outlook for the second half of 1996 and barring unforeseen circumstances, the second-half net result should be in line with the first-half performance,&quot; the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>First-half 1996 group net profit rose 8.6 percent to 7.31 billion francs from 6.73 billion in the first half of 1995.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
